INT. HELIX LABS - OPEN-PLAN OFFICE - NIGHT

SUPER: "DAY 4 OF THE LOCKDOWN"

Standing desks. Beanbags. A neon sign: MOVE FAST. The glass doors are chained from the inside.

IMANI, 30s, sleeves rolled, crouches behind a kombucha fridge. Her breath fogs.

INSERT - HER PHONE

A single bar of signal. Contact: JONAH. Ringing.

Across the floor, TWO TEENAGE INTERNS share a vending-machine bag of chips by a window, whispering. A golden retriever sleeps under a desk, ribs rising and falling.

JONAH (V.O.)
(static, breathing)
Imani. Don't talk. Listen.

IMANI
(whisper)
Where are you?

JONAH (V.O.)
Stairwell. Below you. The thing's in the vents, it follows the heat. Kill the lights on the east side and it moves.

IMANI'S POV - the east wall. A bank of switches. Forty feet of open floor between.

IMANI
That's forty feet in the open.

JONAH (V.O.)
Then run.

She runs. Beanbags, cables, a skateboard she nearly trips on. The dog lifts its head.

Her hand slams the switches. East side DARK.

Silence. Then a metallic scrape in the ceiling, travelling away.

Both interns give her a thumbs up. She almost laughs.

The dog barks once. Sharp. The scraping stops. Reverses.

The stairwell door BURSTS open. JONAH, 30s, bleeding at the temple, stumbles in with a fire axe.

JONAH
(not on the phone anymore)
It was never in the vents.

He looks up. Slowly, so does she.
